nodes.body:
@codex review

Pls focus on the K3 reporting window in `16530ba`: the server-selected suffix now survives batching and typed IPC, and each reusable write interval is projected before usage is serialized. This also covers direct Responses requests and the next request after built-in tools. Physical cache coordinates stay unchanged.

The focused CPU replay passes; large-model candidate GPU validation is still pending. The live H20 27B runs an older package, so its cache-read/streaming baseline is recorded separately.

@codex review

PTAL at `d8406632`. This folds in #46549/#46607 and syncs main's `RequestOutputStats` refactor. Pls focus on the public prompt boundary, unknown vs zero writes, and the per-row write snapshots when request stats are omitted. Physical stats stay unchanged for metrics/traces.

Current-source CPU replays cover the actual Responses/Anthropic generators and typed transport, including metadata-only chunks and a later unknown write. Scoped style and docs checks pass. Full-package, real-cache/GPU and Rust validation remain pending. The [Base gate on this head](https://github.com/sgl-project/sglang/actions/runs/40993347780/job/123860838781) still stops at the missing `run-ci` label; could a maintainer enable the relevant CI after taking a look?

